<% content_for :title, "How I work" %>
<div class="page"><div class="wrap prose">
  <h1>How I work</h1>
  <p>One conversation about one deal. If it isn't useful, you will know in an hour.</p>

  <h3>1. A first conversation</h3>
  <p>You tell me about the deal and the sponsor. I tell you whether technical diligence would change your decision, and what it would cover. There is no charge for this.</p>

  <h3>2. A fixed scope and fee, in writing</h3>
  <p>Before any work starts you know what I will review, what I will not, how long it takes and what it costs. The agreement names the team, including any specialist I bring in.</p>

  <h3>3. The review</h3>
  <p>I do the work myself, not a junior team. I read what the company has built, test what it claims, and ask the questions an engineer would ask that a sponsor's slides do not answer.</p>

  <h3>4. A memo the whole family can read</h3>
  <p>Plain language, no jargon. It says what is real and what is a demo, what breaks at scale, what it costs to fix, and what to ask next. I walk the principals through it on a call, and I answer the questions of whoever disagrees.</p>

  <h3>5. After the decision</h3>
  <p>If you invest, I can stay on as a technical advisor on a monthly retainer, or lead the technology for a defined period inside the company and hand it to the team that stays.</p>

  <h3>Discretion</h3>
  <p>Your deal stays between us. I do not name clients, I do not share what one office tells me with another, and I do not use client information in any other work. Parallex keeps client engagements separate from every other business I run.</p>

  <p><%= link_to "Request an introduction", new_introduction_path, class: "btn" %></p>
</div></div>
